{"resourceIdentifier":"2469","resourceName":"Afforestation and restoration of degraded forests in Eastern Paraguay or Forestal Azul Carbon Project","description":"Forestal Azul S.A. is a company established in 2018 by a German investor (family office) in cooperation with the UNIQUE group. The aim of the company is to establish sustainable reforestation and forest restoration in Eastern Paraguay for the sequestration of carbon and the production of quality timber in a highly deforested landscape. \r\nForestal Azul purchased a property of 2,309 ha in the Department of San Pedro, Eastern Paraguay, in 2018. As most private estates in Eastern Paraguay, the property had undergone intense land use conversion in the past and maintained around 25 % of its surface covered with natural forest, which by then was highly degraded due to unregulated extraction of biomass and poles, hunting, and fires. The condition of the natural forest was not good enough to initiate viable sustainable forest management. As so many other forest fragments in similar condition in the region, these forests are very vulnerable to forest fires. The risk is exacerbated by the lack of incentives for active forest protection and the changing climate that has been displaying longer droughts in recent years. \r\nForestal Azul seeks to establish sustainable forest land use systems adapted to the condition of the land, while at the same time financially viable and competitive. The land use system envisaged by the company is highly diversified and includes the restoration of degraded natural forests, the introduction of silvopastoral systems on implanted pastures, and fast growing eucalypt plantations on the areas used for mechanized soy production.","location":{"latitude":-23.935331,"longitude":-56.583969},"inPublicCommentPeriod":false,"lastPublicCommentPeriod":{"startInclusive":"2021-07-12","endExclusive":"2021-08-12","endInclusive":"2021-08-11"},"attributes":[{"code":"PROJECT_ID","values":[{"type":"string"